globalThis.STORY_ZW_PAL_EN=Object.assign(globalThis.STORY_ZW_PAL_EN||{},{
'子女':{
'紫微':{title:"The people you raise all wear their own crowns",story:"With Zi Wei in your Children palace, the younger people around you, whether kids, students or juniors, tend to have strong opinions and plenty of pride, and they never liked being told what to do. You expect a lot of them and you're willing to back them with resources, but you can end up tying them to your plans with a well-meant “I'm only doing this for you.” Your creative work has standards too: you'd rather go slowly than put out something you aren't proud of.",scenes:["When you train a new hire, you write out every step of the process, and they come back with a different method. Your first reaction is to bristle.","You might pick out tutoring and after-school classes for a child or student, only to hear, “I want to decide for myself.”"],advice:"Give them a small territory where they're in charge. Your job is to be the safety net, not the director."},
'紫微·天府':{title:"A small kingdom with a full granary",story:"With Zi Wei and Tian Fu in your Children palace, your bond with younger people is steady and substantial. You lead people the way you'd run an old family business: you can provide resources and you keep the house rules. They're usually mature and sensible, and as adults they're able to look after you in return. Your blind spot is planning too well, which can rob them of the chance to fall and get back up on their own.",scenes:["When your nephew decides to study abroad, the first thing you open is a spreadsheet, with exchange rates and insurance already worked out.","You might run a side business or partnership smoothly for years and still hesitate to hand it over to a younger partner."],advice:"Pick one thing each year to let go of completely. Let them make the calls while you simply watch."},
'紫微·天相':{title:"A finishing school with strict manners",story:"With Zi Wei and Tian Xiang in your Children palace, you care a great deal about how younger people are brought up and how they present themselves. The ones you raise are usually polite and well behaved, and they won't embarrass you in public. Fairness matters to you, so you want to treat every child or student the same. The lesson here is that you can weigh outside opinion too heavily, until their feelings get buried under “what will people think.”",scenes:["Before a family dinner, you remind the kids to greet the elders first and to keep their phones off the table.","When a student talks back to you in public, you might not be that angry inside, yet you feel you've lost face."],advice:"Ask “what do you think?” before you lay down the rules. That is how good manners become their own."},
'紫微·破軍':{title:"A young king who loves tearing down old walls",story:"With Zi Wei and Po Jun in your Children palace, sparks of reform often fly between you and younger people. They have strong personalities, dislike doing things the old way, and often challenge your methods. Your own creative work leans bold too, and you like to scrap things and start over. Relationships with this pairing swing up and down, and after a fight you often understand each other better. Investments and partnerships can also swing wide, so keep an eye on what they cost you.",scenes:["You carefully plan a family trip, one of the kids says “boring,” and the whole itinerary turns into a camping weekend.","You might delete a half-finished piece and rewrite it from scratch. Your friends are stunned, but you feel it's finally right."],advice:"In an argument, say what you're worried about before you say who gets the final word. They'll be more willing to come closer."},
'紫微·七殺':{title:"A general meets the one who will take over",story:"With Zi Wei and Qi Sha in your Children palace, you lead younger people with a military touch: clear goals, explicit expectations, efficiency first. They're usually independent and bold, and want to strike out on their own early. What you offer is training, not pampering. The blind spot is two stubborn tempers colliding, with neither willing to back down first.",scenes:["Coaching a student on a presentation, you say flatly, “Cut this part. Redo it.” Their eyes go red, and the next day they hand in a better version.","You might argue past midnight with a younger business partner over one decision, and in the end you're the one who gives way."],advice:"After a tough talk, add a word of praise. Hard words need a soft landing if the relationship is going to last."},
'紫微·貪狼':{title:"Mentor and protégé on a glittering stage",story:"With Zi Wei and Tan Lang in your Children palace, time with younger people is lively and fun, with a touch of indulgence. You like taking them out for good food and good times, and showing them the world. Creatively you have taste and know what draws people in. This pairing also brings strong romantic energy, and you want atmosphere in your intimate life. Watch that your love of fun doesn't slide into spoiling them; the boundaries are yours to draw.",scenes:["After a student's exams, you treat them to a great meal and end up talking about life for two hours.","At a party with friends you might get pulled up to sing or host, get more and more into it, and forget you have real work the next day."],advice:"Spoiling them is fine, but agree on one or two lines that can't be crossed, so the fun doesn't turn into trouble."},
'天機':{title:"A curiosity engine that never stops spinning",story:"With Tian Ji in your Children palace, the younger people you raise are clever, quick, and full of questions. Your time together feels like a puzzle game: you take things apart and trade ideas. Traditionally these bonds are few but close, and they shift as circumstances change. {{B:天機:Their ideas are nimble and they're easy to talk with.|They tend to overthink, and plans change often.}}",scenes:["A child or student asks “why is the sky blue?”, you spend half an hour looking it up, and the conversation wanders further and further.","You might start three creative projects at once, get each one halfway, and jump to a new idea."],advice:"Helping them finish one thing is worth more than teaching them ten new ideas."},
'天機·太陰':{title:"The little lamp by a late-night desk",story:"With Tian Ji and Tai Yin in your Children palace, your bond with younger people is sensitive and built on emotional exchange. You pick up on their mood shifts, and they often confide in you. Your creative work has a literary, detailed feel, suited to writing, design, music and other things that need quiet. The blind spot is overthinking: your worries tend to run ahead of your actions.",scenes:["A student texts back “ok,” and you start wondering whether they're upset today.","Inspiration might strike you in the middle of the night, so you get up and write three pages of notes, then feel too shy to show anyone the next day."],advice:"When you're worried, just ask “are you okay?” It takes less energy than playing out ten episodes in your head."},
'天機·巨門':{title:"A debate club that never adjourns",story:"With Tian Ji and Ju Men in your Children palace, your time with younger people is full of conversation, and full of debate. They're articulate and always ask why, often leaving you lost for words. You teach by reasoning and analysis. The challenge is communication: you say a lot and they only remember your tone; they push back once and you want to answer ten times.",scenes:["A talk about whether to buy a new phone turns into a full debate on attitudes toward money.","You might pick apart a partner's proposal line by line in a meeting, win the argument, and lose the mood in the room."],advice:"Halfway through an argument, pause and say “I see what you mean,” then give your version."},
'天機·天梁':{title:"The old master who tells good stories",story:"With Tian Ji and Tian Liang in your Children palace, you're a natural advisor to younger people. You like sharing experience and explaining how things work, and you use stories and metaphors to make it click. They tend to be mature for their age and can hold a real conversation with you. The blind spot is that you can't resist giving advice: sometimes they only want to be heard, and you've already started the lecture.",scenes:["A younger person says work isn't going well, you open with “Let me tell you what I did back when…”, and they quietly start scrolling their phone.","You might be known as “the teacher” in your club or office, and want to answer questions nobody asked you."],advice:"Ask first: “Do you want me to listen, or do you want advice?” Then decide how much to say."},
'太陽':{title:"Pouring all your warmth onto the next generation",story:"With Tai Yang in your Children palace, you're warm and generous with younger people and willing to give them your time and energy. Like a small sun, you show them the world and cheer them on. {{B:太陽:What you give usually comes back, and the relationships stay bright.|You give a lot yet often feel unseen, and it wears you out.}}",scenes:["You planned to rest this weekend, but you still drive a student or your nephew to a competition and cheer from the sidelines until you're hoarse.","You might stay late fixing a new teammate's draft, get no thanks at all, and sigh in the car on the way home."],advice:"Before you light up others, keep some light for yourself. Saying you're tired is nothing to be ashamed of."},
'太陽·太陰':{title:"Day and night taking turns on duty",story:"With Tai Yang and Tai Yin in your Children palace, you show younger people two faces: one moment the energetic coach pushing them forward, the next the attentive listener. The bond has both sides, rational and emotional. The challenge is mood swings: generous today, anxious tomorrow, and they can't quite tell where you stand.",scenes:["In the morning you encourage your child to sign up for a competition; by evening you worry it's too much and ask if they want to rethink it.","When you create, you might race ahead one moment and get stuck endlessly tweaking details the next."],advice:"Write down your principles and keep them fixed. Your feelings can rise and fall, but the rules shouldn't sway with them."},
'太陽·巨門':{title:"The fired-up lecturer at the podium",story:"With Tai Yang and Ju Men in your Children palace, you teach through talk, and your words are both contagious and persuasive. The younger people around you are usually quick and articulate, and your discussions get lively. {{B:太陽:Your words light people up.|Talking too much can turn into nagging or quarrels.}}",scenes:["Coaching a younger person on interview skills, you get more into the role-play than they do and keep going all afternoon.","You might clash with your kid over coming home late: you explain your reasons, they hear you nagging."],advice:"Say the important thing once. The second time, write it down instead; it lands better."},
'太陽·天梁':{title:"The big tree younger people love to shelter under",story:"With Tai Yang and Tian Liang in your Children palace, you're the dependable older sibling in the eyes of younger people. You like caring for and protecting others, and you're happy to step in and shield them from the storm. Teaching, leading teams and community work suit you. The blind spot is caring too much: they get used to leaning on you, and privately you start to feel like an ATM.",scenes:["A student calls you in trouble, and you still drive over in the middle of the night to help sort it out.","You might cover the bill for younger friends several times, then notice everyone now takes it for granted."],advice:"Before you help, ask yourself, “Is this something they need to learn on their own?” Sometimes stepping back is the bigger kindness."},
'武曲':{title:"A precise ruler with hard edges",story:"With Wu Qu in your Children palace, you guide younger people with a focus on practicality and efficiency, and you show love by doing rather than saying. You'll make sure they have what they need materially, but warm words don't come easily. They're usually independent and down to earth. Traditionally these bonds come later in life or are few but close, and they need time to warm up. When Wu Qu sits in a strong position, your strictness becomes their backbone.",scenes:["When your child does badly on a test, your first question is “which ones did you get wrong?” rather than “are you okay?”","You might lay out a detailed savings plan for a younger person, who only wants to talk about a singer they've just discovered."],advice:"Once a week, find a chance to give praise with no agenda attached. The warmth will come back slowly."},
'武曲·天府':{title:"Guarding a solid vault for the next generation",story:"With Wu Qu and Tian Fu in your Children palace, you care about giving younger people a stable foundation, and you have the means and the will to build up resources. The people you raise are usually practical and good with money, and grow into reliable partners. In partnerships and investments you're conservative and think long term. The challenge is being so practical that emotional connection becomes “tell me what you need and I'll buy it.”",scenes:["When a younger relative moves, you send a washing machine, but never ask how they've been lately.","You might open a studio with a friend and log every expense. They say you're too strict; you call it being responsible."],advice:"Add a handwritten card to the gift, so they know you care about them as a person, not just their needs."},
'武曲·天相':{title:"A principled guardian who keeps their word",story:"With Wu Qu and Tian Xiang in your Children palace, you feel responsible for younger people and you do what you say. You'll fight for what they're owed, and you expect them to keep their word in return. The people you raise are usually responsible and know where the lines are. The blind spot is your strong sense of fairness: when settling disputes between younger people, you can coldly rule on who's right and forget to calm their feelings first.",scenes:["Two kids or students get into a fight, and you immediately open an inquiry into who started it. Both walk away feeling wronged.","You might always deliver on promises to a younger person, and when they forget one they made to you, you remember it for a long time."],advice:"Before deciding who's right, ask “how are you both feeling right now?” Fairness is easier to hear after that."},
'武曲·七殺':{title:"An athlete trained by a tough coach",story:"With Wu Qu and Qi Sha in your Children palace, you raise younger people the way you'd train athletes: high standards, little praise, and a sincere wish to see them grow strong. They tend to be fiery and fiercely independent, and want to leave home or stand on their own early. There may be friction, but also mutual respect. Be careful with partnerships and investments; drive needs to come with an eye for risk.",scenes:["A student says they want to quit, you reply “hold on one more week,” they make it through, and later they're the most grateful of all.","You might lock horns with your child over choosing a major for half a year before you both meet in the middle."],advice:"When you're strict, explain why. Once they understand the purpose, they won't remember only the pain."},
'武曲·破軍':{title:"A building site that knocks down and rebuilds at once",story:"With Wu Qu and Po Jun in your Children palace, your bond with younger people often cycles between breaking down and building up. They have strong personalities, charge ahead, and rarely follow your script. Your own creative work and joint ventures lean bold too, and you can pour a lot of resources into experiments. Watch the drain, but once you get through the friction, you often break new ground together.",scenes:["A younger person suddenly announces they're dropping out to start a business. You fume for three days, and on the fourth you start reviewing their business plan.","You might buy a pile of equipment for a creative project and end up using only half of it."],advice:"Set a ceiling you can afford first, and within that line, let them go for it."},
'武曲·貪狼':{title:"A fruit tree that grows sweeter with time",story:"With Wu Qu and Tan Lang in your Children palace, your bond with younger people is like a fruit tree: it needs patient watering early on and grows sweeter later. You lead in a practical way but also know how to enjoy life, and you'll take them out for good food and good fun. Romance and intimacy run warm here, with an appetite for both pleasure and quality. The lesson is not to rush the early years; things get smoother as time goes on.",scenes:["Your new apprentice keeps making mistakes and you nearly give up, then two years later they're your most capable right hand.","You might explore food or fitness together with a younger person until mentor and student become friends."],advice:"Give a relationship three years before you judge it, not three months."},
'天同':{title:"A big kid soaking up the sun with them",story:"With Tian Tong in your Children palace, your bond with younger people is gentle and relaxed, more like friendship. You don't like playing the stern elder; you'd rather play and eat with them. The people you raise are usually easygoing and pleasant to be around. {{B:天同:You enjoy plenty of good fortune and little conflict.|You can spoil them too much and struggle to be firm when it counts.}}",scenes:["Your kid begs for half an hour more of video games, you say “fine, just thirty minutes,” and you end up playing with them for an hour.","You might take students on a day trip, have more fun than they do, and forget about the homework due when you get back."],advice:"Set one or two rules you'll always hold to, so gentleness doesn't turn into anything goes."},
'天同·太陰':{title:"A gentle afternoon tea with the younger generation",story:"With Tian Tong and Tai Yin in your Children palace, you're tender and thoughtful with younger people, like an elder always ready with a cup of something warm. You're good with feelings, and they like to come to you for comfort and to share secrets. Creatively you have an artistic touch, suited to crafts, writing or music. The challenge is caring so much about feelings that the moment they're unhappy, you soften and give way.",scenes:["A student says the homework is too hard, and before you know it you've done most of it for them.","You might lose a night's sleep over a sick cat or a younger friend's breakup."],advice:"Feeling for them is fine, but let them carry one small thing through on their own. They're stronger than you think."},
'天同·巨門':{title:"A pebble hidden in warm water",story:"With Tian Tong and Ju Men in your Children palace, things look peaceful with younger people on the surface, but there's often something left unsaid. You want to be the nice one and avoid conflict, so misunderstandings pile up. They may be sensitive and prone to complaining, and a single remark can stay with you for a long time. The lesson for this pairing is to talk things out; once you do, everything gets lighter.",scenes:["A younger relative forgets your birthday. You say it's fine, then reply to their messages with one word for a week.","You might overhear a student calling you “a pushover.” You smile it off, and feel hurt for days."],advice:"When something bothers you, say it within twenty-four hours, calmly and directly."},
'天同·天梁':{title:"The one everyone calls their honorary aunt or uncle",story:"With Tian Tong and Tian Liang in your Children palace, you have a natural bond with both elders and youngsters. You're gentle and happy to look after people, and younger ones naturally come to you when something happens. You're not strict; you're more like a tree that makes people feel safe. The blind spot is being too easy to ask: people lean on you, and your time fills up with other people's business.",scenes:["A friend's kids have no one to watch them over the holidays, you say yes on the spot, and spend the whole weekend babysitting.","You might be known at work as “the easiest senior to ask,” and end up doing your own work after hours."],advice:"Practice one sentence: “This time doesn't work for me.” Your good standing won't disappear because of it."},
'廉貞':{title:"A small, spirited flame that's hot to handle",story:"With Lian Zhen in your Children palace, your bond with younger people has both tension and warmth. They have strong personalities and their own ideas, and they love and hate without half measures. You care about them a lot, sometimes enough to want control. Lian Zhen is also a secondary romance star, so chemistry and attraction matter in your intimate life. {{B:廉貞:Your passion becomes something that holds people together.|Small things can easily spark conflict.}}",scenes:["Your kid comes home with purple hair. You're stunned at first, then start researching how to keep the color from fading.","You might disagree with a younger partner over one remark and give each other the silent treatment for a month."],advice:"When you really want to step in, first ask yourself whether you're protecting them or protecting your own pride."},
'廉貞·天府':{title:"A family business with house rules",story:"With Lian Zhen and Tian Fu in your Children palace, you guide younger people with planning and method, and you look after their practical needs. The ones you raise are usually steady and sensible, good at keeping what's been built. In partnerships and investments you check the details and don't take risks lightly. The challenge is your love of order: when they want to take their own road, you can feel slighted.",scenes:["Your child says they don't want to take over the family business. You say you respect that, and dinner is very quiet.","You might write a complete rulebook for your club, and new members privately grumble that it's too strict."],advice:"Treat rules as guardrails, not rails. Let them turn freely within the lines."},
'廉貞·天相':{title:"A fair-minded mediator",story:"With Lian Zhen and Tian Xiang in your Children palace, you care about younger people's character and their sense of how to treat others. You're good at handling disputes between them, appealing to both reason and feeling. They're usually courteous and loyal. The blind spot is getting caught in the middle, taking flak from both sides and swallowing your own hurt.",scenes:["Two students fight over group assignments. You talk to each one separately until they make up, and you're too drained to eat dinner.","You might stand up for a younger person in front of the elders, only to have them tell you to mind your own business."],advice:"After mediating, look after your own feelings too. Not every fight is yours to clean up."},
'廉貞·七殺':{title:"A sword forged on the whetstone",story:"With Lian Zhen and Qi Sha in your Children palace, your bond with younger people is forged through friction. They're strong willed and determined, and often go head to head with you. You set high standards and don't shy away from conflict. These relationships are hard work early on, but after being tested they often become the comrades you trust most. In partnerships, watch out for impulsive decisions.",scenes:["A younger person insists on entering a competition you think is too hard. Your objections get nowhere, and you end up helping them train.","You might argue with a young collaborator about whether to change a piece until someone slams the table."],advice:"After a fight, share a meal where you don't talk business, so the relationship has room to breathe."},
'廉貞·破軍':{title:"An experiment that rewrites the rules",story:"With Lian Zhen and Po Jun in your Children palace, things with younger people are always changing. They're rebellious, creative and refuse to be pigeonholed, and they often surprise you. Your own creative work is experimental too, and you're willing to break the mold. Romance and intimacy run hot, with ups and downs. Partnerships and investments can swing hard, so stay within your means.",scenes:["A student hands in a project that ignores the required format entirely. You're annoyed for five minutes, then admit it looks great.","You might decide on a whim to redo your whole studio, and only cool down after spending a hefty sum."],advice:"Sleep on any big change before deciding. Save the impulses for your art and go slower with money and relationships."},
'廉貞·貪狼':{title:"The organizer at the center of the party",story:"With Lian Zhen and Tan Lang in your Children palace, time with younger people is lively and colorful, and you know how to have fun together. You know how to enjoy life and set a mood, and your romantic and intimate life runs strong. Creatively you have an entertainer's instinct for what's fun. The challenge is that when play takes over, relationships can stay shallow, or you can lose your sense of limits around temptation.",scenes:["You take younger friends to night markets and concerts, and they all say you're the most fun grown-up they know.","You might get drawn into a great conversation with someone new at a party and only remember at home that you'd promised to be somewhere else."],advice:"Beyond the fun, set aside one deep one-on-one talk each month. That's how the relationship grows roots."},
'天府':{title:"A storehouse that catches you steadily",story:"With Tian Fu in your Children palace, your bond with younger people is stable, and you do your best to give them solid backing. The ones you raise are usually mature and sensible, and know how to value what they have. In partnerships and investments you're conservative and want security. The blind spot is caring so much about stability that when they want to take a risk, your instinct is to hold them back.",scenes:["A younger person says they want to quit their job and travel for a year. Your first question is, “Do you have enough saved?”","You might prepare a full set of reference materials for a student before they've even started getting ready."],advice:"Let them take small risks now and then. Your job is just to keep the way back open."},
'太陰':{title:"Moonlight at a young person's window",story:"With Tai Yin in your Children palace, your love for younger people is delicate and understated, often shown through quiet care. You feel their moods keenly and worry on their behalf as a result. Creatively you lean emotional and have an eye for beauty. {{B:太陰:The relationships are warm and both sides look out for each other.|You carry a lot inside, and words you can't say stay bottled up.}}",scenes:["Before your child heads out, you quietly slip an extra umbrella and a pack of cookies into their bag.","You might toss and turn all night over a passing complaint from a student."],advice:"Turn your worry into one concrete request, like “text me when you get there.” It's easier on both of you."},
'貪狼':{title:"A playmate who takes younger people on adventures",story:"With Tan Lang in your Children palace, your bond with younger people is multi-talented, lively and fun. You like getting them to try new things, whether sports, food or art. Romance and intimacy run strong, with a taste for both playfulness and the senses. {{B:貪狼:Your talents and charm both shine.|Your enthusiasm tends to fade fast, and play wins out over staying power.}}",scenes:["This year you take a younger friend surfing, next year it's pottery, and the gear fills a whole cabinet.","You might meet lots of interesting young people online, and your weekends are always booked."],advice:"Pick one thing you truly love and practice it together until you're both good at it. That connects you more than trying ten things."},
'巨門':{title:"A classroom that's always in discussion",story:"With Ju Men in your Children palace, you and younger people have a lot to talk about, and quarrels come easily too. They may be sensitive, inquisitive and argumentative, and a single sentence from you can affect them deeply. Your creative work leans toward research and depth of content. {{B:巨門:Your conversations go deep and bring real insight.|Misunderstandings pile up and take patience to untangle.}}",scenes:["You casually say “you've put on a bit of weight,” and your child remembers it for years.","You might spend a whole night arguing with young people online over one opinion."],advice:"Before saying something harsh, wait three seconds and rephrase it as a plain description of fact, without judgment."},
'天相':{title:"The good steward who looks after everyone",story:"With Tian Xiang in your Children palace, your bond with younger people is harmonious and well mannered. You take care of the details of their lives and teach them etiquette. They're usually well behaved and easy to talk to, and they know how to read a room. The blind spot is that you keep the big picture in mind so much that you bend yourself to everyone's needs, and in the end nobody asks if you're tired.",scenes:["At family gatherings you handle the seating and the menu, and you even remember which kid won't eat cilantro.","You might stay up past midnight writing a recommendation letter for a student, who only remembers to say thank you the next day."],advice:"When you schedule time to care for others, schedule time to care for yourself too, and put it in your calendar."},
'天梁':{title:"An old tree that gives shade",story:"With Tian Liang in your Children palace, you're naturally an elder, teacher or protector to younger people. You like giving advice and sharing experience, and you'll step in when they're in trouble. They're usually mature for their age. {{B:天梁:Your care carries weight and earns respect.|You tend to worry too much and can come across as a nag.}}",scenes:["A younger relative is about to sign a lease, and you insist on going along to read it clause by clause.","You might quietly clean up a new hire's mess on your team without your manager ever noticing."],advice:"Let them finish speaking before you advise. Listen first, and your words will carry more weight."},
'七殺':{title:"A young general setting off alone",story:"With Qi Sha in your Children palace, the younger people you raise are independent and opinionated, and want to make their own way early. The bond isn't clingy, but there's a distance built on mutual respect. You lead directly and expect results. {{B:七殺:You stand side by side like comrades in arms.|The relationship can turn cold and hard, short on warmth.}}",scenes:["Your child moves out as soon as they come of age. You say it's great, and feel a hole inside.","A new hire you trained might become a manager elsewhere two years later and come back to have coffee with you, and only then do you realize how much you shaped them."],advice:"Distance isn't the same as coldness. A quick “how are you doing?” now and then means a lot to them."},
'破軍':{title:"A work that's always being revised",story:"With Po Jun in your Children palace, your bond with younger people changes often; they're creative, adventurous and a bit rebellious. Your own creative work and joint ventures lean bold, and you like tearing down the old to start again. This placement asks you to accept that plans rarely survive change. {{B:破軍:Each change brings a breakthrough.|Changes cost a lot, so stay within your means.}}",scenes:["The study plan you carefully mapped out for a younger person changes direction three times in one semester.","You might be nearly done with a creative project, decide it's wrong, and start over completely."],advice:"Allow for change, but before each restart, write down what you learned this time."},
'空':{title:"A door facing the window across the way",story:"When your Children palace has no major star, your bond with younger people is very flexible and strongly shaped by circumstances and their personalities; a reading borrows the major stars from the opposite palace. You don't use one fixed way of guiding people; you adjust to each person. The upside is that you can work with children or students of all temperaments. The challenge is that your own principles aren't clear enough, so you can get pulled along.",scenes:["With a lively student you turn into a comedian; with a quiet one you lower your voice to match.","You might want to start a creative project but keep waiting until a friend is free to do it with you."],advice:"Write down the three principles you care about most when guiding people, an anchor that holds while everything else moves."}
},
'田宅':{
'紫微':{title:"Your own living room is your palace",story:"With Zi Wei in your Property palace, you care a lot about the layout and quality of your home. Your living space should look impressive and orderly, and at home you're used to being the one in charge. Family assets tend to be substantial, and you're willing to pay more for a good place to live. The blind spot is being too particular about appearances, so your family may feel they have to follow your rules even at home.",scenes:["Choosing a sofa, you visit three stores and touch every fabric before deciding.","You might come home to unwashed dishes. You don't say anything, but your family can read it on your face."],advice:"Keep one corner of the home that doesn't have to be tidy, so everyone has somewhere to unwind."},
'紫微·天府':{title:"A castle with a full granary",story:"With Zi Wei and Tian Fu in your Property palace, you have a solid family foundation. You care about living securely and well, and your home often carries a reassuring sense of plenty. Saving is instinctive for you, and this palace is your vault. At home you're like the head steward, keeping track of everything big and small. The lesson is that you crave stability so much you can't bring yourself to replace or throw things out.",scenes:["Your storage room always holds a box of toilet paper and a case of bottled water, better stocked than a corner shop.","You might set aside a fixed sum every month, and watching the balance climb is one of your small joys."],advice:"Clear out the house once a year and give away what you don't use. A vault has to circulate to stay alive."},
'紫微·天相':{title:"A neat and dignified residence",story:"With Zi Wei and Tian Xiang in your Property palace, you like a clean, orderly home with a sense of quality. You're particular about how things are arranged, and guests feel comfortable and well received. At home you value rules and courtesy, and family relations involve keeping face. The blind spot is hiding your frustrations to preserve harmony on the surface.",scenes:["Before guests arrive, you line up the shoes by the door and put a vase of flowers on the table.","So as not to disappoint the elders, you might go home for every holiday as expected, feeling worn out inside."],advice:"Find a quiet moment to bring up what's bothering you at home. Dignity doesn't have to be held up by endurance."},
'紫微·破軍':{title:"A grand house forever under renovation",story:"With Zi Wei and Po Jun in your Property palace, your relationship with home is full of change. You may move often or redecorate often, with a strong urge to transform your space. Family assets may go through a cycle of loss before rebuilding, with you laying the new foundation yourself. At home you have firm opinions and are often the one who decides to change things.",scenes:["Less than two years into a place, you're already studying new floor plans and deciding which wall to knock down.","On a whim you might paint a whole room dark green. Your family is startled; you're delighted."],advice:"Before a big overhaul, list your budget and your must-haves, so the joy of renovating doesn't become money stress."},
'紫微·七殺':{title:"Home is the general's command post",story:"With Zi Wei and Qi Sha in your Property palace, your home runs like a command center, built on efficiency and order. You hold the household up on your own strength and are used to shouldering its big matters. You prefer clean, purposeful design and dislike clutter. The challenge is that the atmosphere at home can get tense because you're so serious, and your family feels like they're still at work.",scenes:["You've ruled that the trash goes out at nine every night, and if someone forgets, you remind them on the spot.","You might plan an entire move by yourself, from packing to setting up the internet."],advice:"When you get home, change into something comfortable, and switch from general mode back to family mode."},
'紫微·貪狼':{title:"A luxurious living room with a bar and a sound system",story:"With Zi Wei and Tan Lang in your Property palace, you like a home that's tasteful and fun. You may have a great sound system, a wine cabinet or a collection, and you know how to enjoy yourself at home. Friends often gather at your place, and you're a warm host. The blind spot is a big appetite for beautiful things, so household spending can easily run over.",scenes:["When friends come over, you bring out your tea or wine collection and tell them where each one came from.","You might save for three months to buy a designer lamp."],advice:"Before a big purchase, leave it in your cart for a week. If you still want it, buy it."},
'天機':{title:"A studio on the move",story:"With Tian Ji in your Property palace, your ties to where you live shift often: you move, switch rooms or rearrange furniture more than most. You like using your head to improve your space and will study storage and flow. {{B:天機:Each change improves the way you live.|You keep feeling it's not good enough and find it hard to settle.}}",scenes:["Every few months you rearrange the living room, and your family can never find the remote.","You might have a folder of saved organizing videos and spend weekends testing new methods at home."],advice:"Ask your family before changing things, so the home evolves for everyone, not just as your experiment."},
'天機·太陰':{title:"A small study with moonlight by the window",story:"With Tian Ji and Tai Yin in your Property palace, you like a quiet home with atmosphere: the lighting, the view, a little desk in a corner all matter. You're attentive at home and notice your family's moods. Tai Yin is the natural ruler of this palace, so this pairing brings a deep attachment to home, yet Tian Ji adds movement, and you may relocate several times.",scenes:["Your favorite thing is turning off the overhead light at night and reading by a single warm lamp.","You might bring one particular old piece of furniture with you every time you move, because it's your sense of security."],advice:"Keep a corner of the home that's yours alone, and go sit there when your mind is unsettled."},
'天機·巨門':{title:"An old apartment with thin walls",story:"With Tian Ji and Ju Men in your Property palace, home is full of topics and opinions. Family members discuss a lot and argue a lot, and everyone thinks they're right. You may move, or the place itself may have small issues to watch, such as soundproofing or plumbing. At home you like to analyze, and you tend to overthink.",scenes:["The family debates whether to replace the fridge for two weeks without reaching a decision.","You might hear footsteps upstairs in the middle of the night and start drafting a note in your head."],advice:"Set a decision day for big household matters. Discuss until then, then commit, instead of letting it drag."},
'天機·天梁':{title:"An old house full of family stories",story:"With Tian Ji and Tian Liang in your Property palace, your home often carries the presence of elders: you may be looked after by family or live in a house with history. At home you like being the one with ideas, and everyone comes to you when something's up. You prefer spaces with books and tea, where you can sit still and think. The challenge is that the family has many opinions, and you're often the one called in to mediate.",scenes:["The family group chat is debating where to have the holiday dinner, and in the end everyone waits for your word.","You might keep your grandfather's old desk even though the edges are worn smooth."],advice:"When mediating family matters, just put forward options, and let everyone share the final decision."},
'太陽':{title:"A house full of daylight",story:"With Tai Yang in your Property palace, you like a bright, open, lively home. You're warm at home, often invite friends over, and give a lot to your family. The mood at home is shaped more by your father or male elders. {{B:太陽:The household is bright and you have a strong presence at home.|You give a lot and get little back, and the chores tend to land on you.}}",scenes:["When viewing a place, the first thing you do is open the curtains to see how much sun comes in.","You might cook a huge spread for friends every weekend and eat last yourself."],advice:"Share the housework. Your warmth is a strength, not a reason to carry everything."},
'太陽·太陰':{title:"A home lit by sun by day and moon by night",story:"With Tai Yang and Tai Yin in your Property palace, your home holds both a lively and a quiet atmosphere. Both parents shape you deeply, and you carry the family's strength and softness alike. You want your space bright by day and cozy by night. The challenge is that your mood follows the mood at home, and family discord hits you especially hard.",scenes:["Your living room has a big window, but your bedroom must have blackout curtains.","You might soothe both sides when family members fight, then slip out to the balcony alone for some air."],advice:"Your family's feelings aren't all your responsibility. After calming things down, let yourself rest too."},
'太陽·巨門':{title:"A debate over the dinner table",story:"With Tai Yang and Ju Men in your Property palace, home is a place of blunt talk and lots of discussion, lively but quick to spark arguments. You like to explain your reasoning at home and care whether your family actually listened. You value shared spaces and like a big dining table and a big living room. {{B:太陽:Discussion becomes real exchange.|Discussion can easily turn into fighting.}}",scenes:["A news story comes up at dinner, everyone takes a side, and the meal lasts two hours.","You might tell your family “I'm just saying,” when you've already said it three times."],advice:"Make mealtimes a no-argument zone and save contentious topics for after dinner."},
'太陽·天梁':{title:"The ancestral home the whole clan returns to",story:"With Tai Yang and Tian Liang in your Property palace, your home enjoys the protection of elders and a tradition of caring for others. You're the one who holds things together at home, and the family often calls on you when something comes up. You like spacious homes that can take in lots of people. The challenge is looking after family so much that your own needs come last.",scenes:["At the big holiday gathering, you pick up the elders, prepare the gift envelopes and arrange the seating.","You might keep a guest room ready, and relatives come to stay every so often."],advice:"Keep some time at home that's yours alone. Look after yourself before you look after others."},
'武曲':{title:"A safe built for practicality",story:"With Wu Qu in your Property palace, you want a home that's practical, durable and easy to keep clean. You have a saver's instinct; this palace is your vault, and building assets through your own effort is your path. The mood at home may lean rational, with few sweet words. {{B:武曲:You're excellent at building savings.|Watch for money arguments at home.}}",scenes:["Buying appliances, you always compare prices and warranties, and run the numbers three times in your head before spending.","You might move a sum into savings the moment your paycheck lands each month."],advice:"The household budget can be strict, but keep some money for “things that make us happy.” That's what gives a home warmth."},
'武曲·天府':{title:"A solid, reliable family vault",story:"With Wu Qu and Tian Fu in your Property palace, you have real confidence when it comes to wealth reserves. You're good at holding on to money and saving, and your household usually has a stable financial base. At home you're practical and value security and planning. You like solid, well-made things. The blind spot is guarding too tightly, so you can pour cold water on family members who want to spend on enjoyment.",scenes:["When your family wants a new sofa, you first ask, “How many more years will the old one last?”","You might keep the household accounts in perfect order and save every receipt."],advice:"Holding on is a skill. Spending now and then on your family's happiness builds another kind of reserve."},
'武曲·天相':{title:"The steward who keeps the books spotless",story:"With Wu Qu and Tian Xiang in your Property palace, you run the household in an orderly way, with rules for how money is spent and where things go. You're responsible at home and often the one handling rent, bills and payments. With family assets you value fairness and care whether the division is reasonable. The challenge is being so rule-bound that your family feels you're auditing them.",scenes:["Sharing a flat, you make a spreadsheet that splits everyone's utilities down to the decimal.","You might insist that every item be written down clearly when the family discusses dividing assets."],advice:"Once the rules are set, stop checking every day. Give your family some trust."},
'武曲·七殺':{title:"A house you built yourself",story:"With Wu Qu and Qi Sha in your Property palace, you'll mostly build your home through your own hard work, and you may have moved around in your early years. At home you're efficient and decisive and used to handling big things alone. You prefer simple, highly functional spaces. The challenge is an atmosphere that leans hard, short on soft, easy connection.",scenes:["On moving day you carry twenty boxes yourself, and by the time friends arrive to help you've finished unpacking.","When you get home, you might plan out tomorrow before you'll let yourself sit down."],advice:"Bring some soft things into your home, a plant or a throw blanket, so you can relax too."},
'武曲·破軍':{title:"A plot that's torn down and rebuilt",story:"With Wu Qu and Po Jun in your Property palace, your relationship with where you live and with family assets keeps breaking down and building up. You may go through moves, renovations or a reorganization of household finances. You're willing to make changes at home and don't mind the hassle. Saving with this pairing takes discipline, since spending on the home can easily run over.",scenes:["You meant to replace a faucet, and ended up redoing the whole bathroom.","One year you might suddenly clear out most of your belongings and switch to a completely new style."],advice:"Set a cap for home projects. Anything over it waits until next season."},
'武曲·貪狼':{title:"A piggy bank that grows slowly",story:"With Wu Qu and Tan Lang in your Property palace, your relationship with home improves with time. Early on your place may be modest and saving hard, but you have staying power and know how to enjoy life, and as the years go by the quality of your home rises noticeably. At home you like things with entertainment value, such as good kitchen gear or audio-visual equipment.",scenes:["Fresh out of school you live in a tiny studio, yet you still buy a good coffee machine.","You might save a little each year to add one thing to your home that makes you happy."],advice:"Keep enjoyment and savings in two separate accounts. Look after both, and your home keeps getting better."},
'天同':{title:"A comfy beanbag",story:"With Tian Tong in your Property palace, your top requirement for home is comfort and ease. The atmosphere is usually happy, and you're easy to live with, the one who helps everyone relax. {{B:天同:Home life runs smoothly and comfortably.|You can get lazy, household chores keep getting put off, and saving isn't a priority.}}",scenes:["On weekends you can spend the whole day at home in pajamas, watching shows, snacking and napping.","You might have been saying you'll sort out the wardrobe for three months, and the clothes are still piled on a chair."],advice:"Set one small goal a week, like tidying a single drawer. Comfort and order can live together."},
'天同·太陰':{title:"A home with warm light and hot soup",story:"With Tian Tong and Tai Yin in your Property palace, your home is warm and soft, a place of real security. You care about the atmosphere and use lighting, scents and cushions to make it cozy. Tai Yin rules this palace, so your attachment to home runs deep and your saving tends to be steady. The challenge is being such a homebody that you lose some drive for the world outside.",scenes:["Almost every light in your home is warm yellow, and friends say it feels like a café.","You might start missing your own bed by day five of a trip abroad."],advice:"Home is a charging station, not your whole shelter. Get out regularly, and you'll love it even more when you come back."},
'天同·巨門':{title:"Small ripples under a calm surface",story:"With Tian Tong and Ju Men in your Property palace, home looks peaceful but holds quite a few things left unsaid. Small misunderstandings and complaints build up between family members until they become knots. You want peace at home, so you often choose silence. Also keep an eye on small issues with the house itself, like damp or noise.",scenes:["Someone in the family moves your things. You don't say anything, but you remember.","You might notice mold starting in a corner of the bathroom and put off dealing with it for two months."],advice:"Deal with small things at home while they're small, whether it's words or a damp corner. Don't wait for them to grow."},
'天同·天梁':{title:"A warm family home under the elders' protection",story:"With Tian Tong and Tian Liang in your Property palace, your home is blessed and looked after by elders. The family mood is mostly happy, and everyone helps each other. At home you're gentle and easy to talk to, a safe harbor for your family. You like quiet, green places. The challenge is relying on family too much or deferring to elders so much that your own space shrinks.",scenes:["You live close to your parents, and every few days someone drops off food.","You might want to replace the old curtains, but haven't because an elder picked them."],advice:"Thank your family for their care, and gently say how you'd like things to be. Your home can have your style too."},
'廉貞':{title:"A house with a story",story:"With Lian Zhen in your Property palace, your relationship with home has tension, and there may be some complicated feelings within the family. You hold firm to your own preferences at home and have a strong need to control your space. You like design with character. {{B:廉貞:Home is a source of energy for you.|Friction comes easily at home and takes extra patience to manage.}}",scenes:["You insist the walls be painted a particular color, and won't budge even when the family objects.","You might disagree with your siblings for quite a while over what to do with the old family house."],advice:"In family conflicts, deal with the feelings first and the issue second. Get the order right and it's easier to talk."},
'廉貞·天府':{title:"A well-run family accounts office",story:"With Lian Zhen and Tian Fu in your Property palace, you run a household well, both planning and preserving. You handle domestic matters in an orderly way and you're good at saving. You value stability and order at home and feel responsible for family assets. The blind spot is a need for control that leaves your family feeling micromanaged.",scenes:["Every shelf in your fridge has an assigned purpose, and you notice when anyone puts something in the wrong place.","You might put together a list of all your parents' insurance policies and accounts, and the whole family relies on you for it."],advice:"Manage the big picture and let your family decide the small details. They'll cooperate more willingly."},
'廉貞·天相':{title:"A family council that insists on fairness",story:"With Lian Zhen and Tian Xiang in your Property palace, you value fairness and rules at home and want family matters spelled out clearly. You often play the coordinator, stepping in when disputes break out. You like a neat, orderly home. The challenge is that, caught between relatives, you can end up pleasing no one while holding back your own feelings.",scenes:["The schedule for which sibling looks after your parents and when is one you drew up.","You might spend three days coordinating in the group chat over where to hold a family gathering."],advice:"Coordinating is helping, not an obligation. When you're tired, ask someone else to take over."},
'廉貞·七殺':{title:"A home that keeps breaking new ground",story:"With Lian Zhen and Qi Sha in your Property palace, you may have to fight to build your home, and you may have moved in your early years. At home you're strong willed and used to deciding and carrying things yourself. You prefer spaces with character and strong function. The challenge is that your forcefulness can make the atmosphere at home tense.",scenes:["You canvass several neighborhoods on your own and won't sign a lease until you find the place that feels right.","You might make a decision at home and only tell everyone afterward."],advice:"Hold a small family meeting before major household decisions. Letting everyone take part removes a lot of resistance."},
'廉貞·破軍':{title:"A renovation that keeps starting over",story:"With Lian Zhen and Po Jun in your Property palace, your relationship with where you live changes often: you may move and remodel many times, and family assets may go through changes too. You have a strong eye for aesthetics and an urge to transform your space, and you hate things staying the same. Saving takes discipline with this pairing, as home spending can turn impulsive.",scenes:["You see a Scandinavian-style photo and the next week replace all the living room furniture.","You might move so often that friends say, “That's the fourth time I've updated your address.”"],advice:"Before each big change, ask yourself whether you want a new space or a new life."},
'廉貞·貪狼':{title:"A lively private club",story:"With Lian Zhen and Tan Lang in your Property palace, your home is lively and entertaining, decorated with atmosphere and often full of friends. You know how to enjoy yourself at home and have standards for food, music and lighting. The challenge is that household spending gets pulled along by desire, and with so much of your life happening outside, your living situation may change more often.",scenes:["You have a whole wall of wine or collectible figures, and friends always take photos.","You might host parties at home often and be cleaning up until midnight afterward."],advice:"Set a monthly budget for fun and stop when it's spent, so home stays a happy place."},
'天府':{title:"A granary filled to the brim",story:"With Tian Fu in your Property palace, the treasury star sits in the palace of reserves, and you have a natural knack for holding on to money and saving. Your household usually has a stable financial base, and you value security at home. You're like a steward who keeps everything in order. If Tian Fu is joined by void or malefic stars, the vault can spring a leak, so take care to keep it secure.",scenes:["Your storage is so systematic that you could find anything with your eyes closed.","You might review your household spending once a year to see where you can save more."],advice:"While building your reserves, let money carry some warmth too, and use it to make your family's life better."},
'太陰':{title:"The gentlest moonlight under your roof",story:"Tai Yin is the natural ruler of the Property palace, so its presence here is felt strongly. You have deep feelings for home, care about atmosphere, and are strongly influenced by the women elders in your family. At home you're attentive and caring, and you like a quiet life. {{B:太陰:Home life is stable and you're good at saving.|You tend to worry about family matters, and your mood rises and falls with the household.}}",scenes:["Your most relaxed moment is after a shower at night, reading in bed while listening to the rain.","You might remember what everyone at home likes to eat and pick it up whenever you shop."],advice:"Treat home as a place to recharge, and allow yourself times when you don't have to look after anyone."},
'貪狼':{title:"A house full of collections",story:"With Tan Lang in your Property palace, you like your home to be fun and full, perhaps with lots of collections and hobby gear. You know how to entertain yourself at home and like inviting friends over. {{B:貪狼:Home is lively and life has flavor.|Things pile up, spending scatters, and saving is hard.}}",scenes:["You have one cabinet just for board games and another for souvenirs from your travels.","The first thing you might do when you get home is turn on the music so the house isn't silent."],advice:"Declutter once a season and leave the space for the things you truly love."},
'巨門':{title:"A house that needs more open windows",story:"With Ju Men in your Property palace, arguments come easily at home, and communication between family members needs extra care. With housing, watch for hidden problems such as poor light, plumbing or noisy neighbors. {{B:巨門:Home is talkative, but once things are talked through you grow closer.|Misunderstandings build up and need more patience.}}",scenes:["When viewing a place, you check the corners for water stains and listen for noise from upstairs.","You might get into a fight with family over one remark and realize afterward it was a misunderstanding."],advice:"Slow down when you talk at home, and ask “Do you mean…?” It prevents a lot of fights."},
'天相':{title:"A well-kept residence",story:"With Tian Xiang in your Property palace, you like a clean, orderly home and care about quality of living. Family interactions are courteous, and you often take on the role of looking after everyone. Tian Xiang brings comfort in food and clothing, so home life usually lacks little. {{B:天相:Home is harmonious and elders look out for you.|You tend to bend yourself to accommodate your family.}}",scenes:["There's always a little table by your front door for keys, mail and a small vase of flowers.","You might always volunteer to wash up at family gatherings, and everyone says you're the most thoughtful."],advice:"Let your family see what you give now and then. Saying “your turn this time” is perfectly normal."},
'天梁':{title:"The family home in the shade of an old tree",story:"With Tian Liang in your Property palace, your home often enjoys the protection of elders: you may live in a family property or have relatives help you settle. At home you're the head of the family, happy to look after people, and everyone comes to you with their problems. {{B:天梁:The family's blessings run deep and home life is steady.|The duty of care weighs heavily, and you can end up carrying too much family business.}}",scenes:["The old house still has your childhood height marks carved into the door frame.","You might get called in to fix the elders' phones or fill out their paperwork every time you visit."],advice:"Help with family matters, but don't take on everything. Let others share some of the load."},
'七殺':{title:"A tent you can pitch on your own",story:"With Qi Sha in your Property palace, you'll mostly build your home through your own efforts, and you may move around. At home you're independent and opinionated and dislike interference. You prefer simple, crisp spaces. {{B:七殺:Your own ability builds you a solid home.|There's more change, and building up takes more patience.}}",scenes:["Renting on your own for the first time, you handle everything yourself, from finding the place to negotiating to moving.","You might keep your home so minimal that friends say it looks like a hotel."],advice:"Home is more than a place to sleep. Invite a few friends over now and then to give it some life."},
'破軍':{title:"A home that's always on a new version",story:"With Po Jun in your Property palace, your ties to where you live are changeable: you may move or renovate often, and family assets may go through loss before renewal. You love novelty and don't cling to old things. {{B:破軍:Every change is an upgrade.|Changes cost a lot, and saving takes stronger discipline.}}",scenes:["In one year you rearrange your room twice and sell all the old furniture online.","You might see a neighborhood you like and start seriously considering moving there."],advice:"Work out the cost before you change things. Novelty is worth chasing, but only if you can afford the chase."},
'空':{title:"A room waiting to be furnished",story:"When your Property palace has no major star, a reading borrows the stars of the opposite palace. Your relationship with home is very flexible and strongly shaped by circumstances and the people you live with. You can adapt to all kinds of living situations and make a home anywhere. The upside is adaptability; the challenge is that the shape of your home is often decided by others, and your own needs get overlooked.",scenes:["Sharing a flat, you go along with your roommates on the living room layout and only arrange your own room.","You might live somewhere for years with bare walls, always thinking you'll decorate later."],advice:"Make one decision at home just for you, even if it's only a painting or a lamp, so the place carries your mark."}
}
});
